  {"id":"abstract_hip_hop","name":"Abstract hip hop","family":"hip_hop","lineage":"Late-1990s and 2000s independent hip-hop emphasizing associative imagery and densely constructed MC writing. Aesop Rock and Blockhead’s Labor Days (2001), issued through Definitive Jux, anchors the selected New York sample-based strand. Abstract describes the writing and approach, rather than a single production technology; this authored studio recipe selects an articulate solo flow and chopped sample bed.","instruments":["voice","sampler_drum_machine","sampler_classic"],"room":"treated_studio","tuning":"twelve_tet","chain_archetype":"arch_modern_pro_daw_studio","chain_mic":"condenser_fet","chain_pre":"transformerless","chain_console":"console_in_the_box","chain_comp":"comp_fet","chain_eq":"eq_active_parametric","chain_medium":"digital_std","chain_status":"authored_studio_model","pin_parts":true,"parts":{"voice_register":"chest_voice","voice_quality":"rap_voice","voice_speech_song":"voice_rhythmic_spoken_flow","voice_tradition":"voice_tradition_source_unspecified","voice_vibrato":"straight_tone","voice_microtone":"tempered_voice","voice_pitch_organization":"voice_pitch_equal_tempered_12","voice_ornament_system":"voice_ornament_none","voice_mechanism_compound":"voice_mechanism_single_source","voice_estill_quality":"voice_estill_speech","voice_processing_chain":"voice_processing_unprocessed","voice_ensemble_config":"voice_ensemble_solo_accompanied","electronic_technique":"electronic_sample_chopped","sample_bitdepth":"sixteen_bit","sample_swing":"mid_swing","sample_processing":"chopped_break","sampler_classic_context":"sampler_classic_hiphop","sampler_bit_depth":"sampler_sixteen_bit","sampler_archetypes":"ensoniq_asr10","sampler_workflow":"sampler_chopped_breaks","voice_articulation":"narrative_voice","voice_multitrack_stack":"voice_multitrack_single_lead"}},
  {"id":"alternative_hip_hop","name":"Alternative hip hop","family":"hip_hop","lineage":"A broad alternative hip-hop designation encompassing departures from dominant rap conventions in subject matter, sample selection and song form. This recipe selects the late-1980s Long Island / New York sample-collage strand of De La Soul and Prince Paul’s 3 Feet High and Rising (1989), with playful MC exchanges, layered breaks and interludes. The selected configuration is not a sonic definition of every alternative hip-hop artist.","instruments":["voice","sampler_drum_machine","sampler_classic","turntable"],"room":"treated_studio","tuning":"twelve_tet","chain_archetype":"arch_80s_indie_commercial_us","chain_mic":"condenser_fet","chain_pre":"pre_console_inline_strip","chain_console":"console_british_class_a_70s","chain_comp":"comp_dbx_160_vca","chain_eq":"eq_console_surgical","chain_medium":"tape_30ips","chain_status":"authored_studio_model","pin_parts":true,"parts":{"voice_register":"chest_voice","voice_quality":"rap_voice","voice_speech_song":"voice_rhythmic_spoken_flow","voice_tradition":"voice_tradition_source_unspecified","voice_vibrato":"straight_tone","voice_microtone":"tempered_voice","voice_pitch_organization":"voice_pitch_equal_tempered_12","voice_ornament_system":"voice_ornament_none","voice_mechanism_compound":"voice_mechanism_single_source","voice_estill_quality":"voice_estill_speech","voice_processing_chain":"voice_processing_unprocessed","voice_ensemble_config":"voice_ensemble_call_response_leader_group","electronic_technique":"electronic_sample_chopped","sample_bitdepth":"twelve_bit","sample_swing":"heavy_swing","sample_processing":"chopped_break","sampler_classic_context":"sampler_classic_hiphop","sampler_bit_depth":"sampler_twelve_bit","sampler_archetypes":"emu_sp1200","sampler_workflow":"sampler_loop_layered","voice_articulation":"call_response_voice","voice_multitrack_stack":"voice_multitrack_adlib_response_lane","turntable_technique":"turntable_chirp_baby"}}